6. **Performance Considerations** – Readers incur only an RCU read lock/unlock pair (no mutex contention). Writers pay only the cost of allocating new nodes and scheduling deferred frees.
7. **Cleanup** – When the module is unloaded or the system shuts down, iterate over all allocated nodes using `list_*` helpers and invoke `call___rcu(&node->rcu)` for each.
